OL,3,GNEWSADover Castle and its headless
OL,4,Adrummer boy
OL,5,
OL,6,FIf you visit Dover Castle, you might
OL,7,Fhear the faint sound of drumming.
OL,9,FAccording to legend, the fortress known
OL,10,Fas "the key to England", due to its
OL,11,Fstrategic defense spot, is haunted by
OL,12,Fboth King Charles I and a child - the
OL,13,Fheadless drummer boy.
OL,15,FGavin Wright, visitor assistant for
OL,16,FEnglish Heritage at the Kent site, said
OL,17,Fthe story was that a young drummer boy
OL,18,Fwas sent to collect soldiers' wages and
OL,19,Fmurdered by robbers on his way back to
OL,20,Fthe castle, with his head never being
OL,21,Ffound.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
